[b]Better Zoom - 1.1.0[/b]
Zoom further out and in with the normal mouse wheel, in the workshop and research tree.

[b]Unlock Better Zoom[/b]
Open [b]Tech Tree → Mods[/b] and research [b]Better Zoom[/b] for [b]100 gold[/b]. This unlocks the extra zoom range in the workshop and both research tabs. Until then, normal zoom limits apply. Existing kingdoms also need to purchase this research.

[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[*]Three extra zoom-out steps show up to eight times the normal visible width and height.[/*]
[*]Three extra zoom-in steps provide up to eight times the normal maximum magnification.[/*]
[*]Zoom stays centered under your cursor.[/*]
[*]The research-tree background fills the screen at far zoom and while panning.[/*]
[*]Configure extra steps independently in each direction, from 0 to 5.[/*]
[*]Keyboard panning and Shift+wheel workshop switching retain their usual controls.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Requirements[/b]
Kingdom Inc. for Windows x64 (Mono).
BepInEx 5 for Windows x64.
Foundation 0.5.0 or later, installed separately.

[b]Installation[/b]
1. Install BepInEx and Foundation separately.
2. Close Kingdom Inc.
3. Extract the ZIP into the folder containing KingdomInc.exe.
4. Confirm BepInEx/plugins/BetterZoom/BetterZoom.dll exists.
5. Launch the game, open Tech Tree → Mods, and research Better Zoom.

[b]Configuration[/b]
After the first launch, close the game and edit BepInEx/config/urakka.kingdominc.betterzoom.cfg:
ExtraZoomOutLevels = 3
ExtraZoomInLevels = 3
Each extra step doubles or halves magnification. Choose 0 through 5 independently for each direction, then restart. Zero retains the normal limit in that direction. Research is required before extra steps take effect.

[b]Updating and removal[/b]
Close the game before replacing the DLL. To remove Better Zoom, delete BepInEx/plugins/BetterZoom and optionally its configuration file. Saved kingdoms remain usable.
The research unlock is saved with your kingdom. Extended views are temporary; reopening a view or restarting may restore a normal zoom level.

At far zoom, text and buildings become small. The background grid becomes coarser to fill the view. Keyboard panning uses the speed of the nearest normal zoom level.

[b]Changes in 1.1.0[/b]
Add Better Zoom research under Tech Tree → Mods for 100 gold, unlocking the extra zoom range.

[b]Source and support[/b]
[url=https://github.com/urakkaamyx/KingdomInc_BetterZoom]Source code, documentation and support[/url].
Created for rockyamyx / urakkaamyx with AI-generated code, page text and promotional artwork.
